\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1.\cf0  Commit thy way, confiding,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 when trials here arise,
\par to Him whose hand is guiding
\par the tumults of the skies.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par There clouds and tempests raging
\par have each their paths assigned;
\par Will God for thee engaging
\par no way of safety find?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2.  Trust in the Lord, thy Saviour,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 who for thy want's provides.
\par Build on His grace and favour,
\par thy work shall safe abide.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Thou can't make no advances
\par by self consuming care,
\par but He His help dispenses
\par When called upon in pray'r.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3.  His way the only pathway,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 all pow'r is in His hand.
\par His gracious works our mainstay,
\par in thankfulness we stand
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par His work on man can hinder,
\par His labours ne'er can rest
\par Until all of His chilren
\par eternally are blessed.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  Arise! Forget thy sorrow,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 thy troubles, fears and pain.
\par Be trusting that the morrow
\par \pard     will bring eternal gain!
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1 For thou art not the ruler\cf0 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Who reigns and governs all,
\par Our Lord and heav'nly Master
\par helps us and hears our call.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Let Him then rule and guide thee,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 for He is wise and just.
\par In all truth He will lead thee,
\par so place in Him thy trust!
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Beyond thy wish extended
\par His goodness will appear
\par When He hath fully ended
\par \pard    What caused thy needless fear.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

